            <div xml:id="d966">

                <pb facs="0863" n="856" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.94244/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-01T12:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1937—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>103. Your 191, June 30, 1 p.m. The Department authorizes the Embassy to make
                    informally appropriate representations to the Chinese Foreign Office in regard
                    to the adverse effects, on the business of <pb facs="0864" n="857"
                        xml:id="pg857"/> the interested American firms, of smuggling into North
                    China of kerosene and gasoline, but feels that the Embassy should avoid making a
                    specific suggestion that a preventive office be established at the Tientsin East
                    Station. However, the Department perceives no objection to the making of such a
                    suggestion by the companies themselves should they desire to do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
